{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he saw the Kenite.</b> Because the Kenite was settled among Amalek, as it says ״וַיֹּאמֶר שָׁאוּל אֶל הַקֵּינִי״ etc. (I Samuel 15), he mentioned him after Amalek. He reflected upon the greatness of the children of Jethro, for it is said of them (II Chronicles 2) ״תִּרְעָתִים שִׁמְעָתִים סוּכָתִים״ (Sifrei Numbers 10; Sanhedrin 104)." "<b>Your dwelling-place is enduring.</b> I marvel — how did you merit this? Were you not with me in the counsel of ״הָבָה נִתְחַכְּמָה לוֹ״ (Exodus 1), and now you have settled in the enduring stronghold of Israel? (Sanhedrin 106)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:37.926202574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}